The web board, worker/src/web/board.js, ports two pieces of MIT-licensed code,
each under its own licence below: its eased reordering animation (each card's
place measured before and after a move, then animated from the old place to the
new, from the place it is shown at while an earlier move still runs) and its
midpoint rule for where a dragged card lands come from SortableJS 1.15.7
(https://github.com/SortableJS/Sortable, src/Animation.js and src/Sortable.js),
redone with the Web Animations API; its keyboard dragging (Space lifts, the
arrows move, Space, Enter or Tab drops, Escape cancels) and its screen-reader
announcements follow dnd-kit's @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1
(https://github.com/clauderic/dnd-kit, packages/core/src/sensors/keyboard and
packages/core/src/components/Accessibility).

The panel's pickers in Manage, worker/src/web/panel.js's combo(), port the
keyboard model of GitHub's @github/combobox-nav 3.0.2 (MIT,
https://github.com/github/combobox-nav, commit
d99492419e8943b43cd1a61b851f46ecccbdf595, src/index.ts): the arrows move the
active option through aria-activedescendant and wrap, Enter or a click commits
it, Escape closes the list, keys are ignored while an input method composes,
and the first match is made active as you type; under its licence below.

Each person's disc, worker/src/web/avatar.js, ports the "marble" variant of
boring-avatars 2.0.4 (MIT, https://github.com/boringdesigners/boring-avatars,
commit 89270f1d423a60a2fa2c241127e1744cba38aa38, the npm package's
dist/index.js): its name hash, its shapes,
offsets, scales, rotations and blur, drawn as a plain SVG string from the
username in P99's palette; under its licence below.

Each board's card order, worker/src/order.js, ports generateKeyBetween and
generateNKeysBetween from rocicorp's fractional-indexing 3.2.0
(https://github.com/rocicorp/fractional-indexing, commit
9e55f979db216df7d20e2be17fbe185d881e3c90, src/index.js): its base-62 digits,
its integer and fraction parts and its midpoint rule. That code is dedicated to
the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal and asks for no notice; it is credited
here all the same.

The images in docs/images/ are made from this repository's own sources, and
are licensed with the code. inbox.gif and setup.gif are recorded by prec
from the shots in render/terminal.toml (p99 tui --demo on sample data, and
p99 setup on the mock account in render/mock-cloudflare.mjs) and made GIFs by
pcod; thread.png, codes.png and list-json.png are prec stills of the shots of
the same names; architecture.png is rendered from render/architecture.svg.
flow.gif joins render/web/record.mjs's frame-exact recording of the web panel
on the sample shop in render/web/site/ with prec's arrives shot, made a GIF by
pcod; panel-light.png, panel-dark.png, badge-light.png, badge-dark.png and
capture.png are that script's stills of the same shop, all on sample data;
verify-light.png and verify-dark.png are its stills of the authenticator prompt,
and invite-totp.png is a prec still of the shot of the same name, on a local Worker.
pitomd.gif, pitomd-corner.png, pitomd-corner-scrolled.png, pitomd-panel-light.png
and pitomd-panel-dark.png are render/web/pitomd.mjs's frame-exact recording and
stills of P99 on the Splicer page of PITO MD's own site, pitomd.com, served by
its dev server, with a local P99 Worker on sample data; the clip is joined with
prec's arrives shot and made a GIF by pcod. The page they show is PITO MD's own
site, © Catalin Ilinca, and is not covered by P99's licences.
web-sizes-bars.png, web-times-bars.png and tui-frames-bars.png are drawn by
pito-compare (pcmp) from the measurements in render/charts/.

